#
# This is an intentially minimalistic obj file that helps show a number of things:
#
# 1. Primary use: axis orientation - there are 3 triangles forming 3 "arrows", pointing in axis directions.
#    The big arrow points in the X direction, then mdeium arrow points to positive Y, the smallest points in positive Z
#    So,
#
#    *** loading this file into a program will let you know how that program interprets XYZ from obj files ***
#
#    ie does the X arrow point to the right?  Is the Y arrow up or is Z up? Or down? etc
#
# 1.b Also, the arrows/triangles are 1 unit in length. So this gives you some sense of how a unit is interpretted
#
# 2. UV mapping - loading a texture should map the center of the texture to the center of the axes
#    the UV map is essentially the 3 triangles, but Y and Z are folded down along their "hinge" with the X arrow:
#
#    +---------+---------+
#    |        /|         |
#    |       / |--__     |
#    |      / Y| X  --__ |
#    |     +---+---------+
#    |         |Z/       |
#    |         | |       |
#    |         |/        |
#    +---------+---------+
#

#
# vertices
# one for each unit direction: x, y, z
#
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 0.0 1.0 0.0
v 0.0 0.0 1.0
# and the origin:
v 0.00000 0.0000 0.000000
# and these will help form triangles of different sizes:
v 0.0 0.6 0.0
v 0.0 0.0 0.45
v 0.3 0.0 0.0

#
# normals, pointing in the base directions
#
vn 1.0 0.0 0.0
vn 0.0 1.0 0.0
vn 0.0 0.0 1.0

#
# texture UV coords
#
# 0.0 0.0 is BOTTOM-left of texture, 1.0 1.0 is TOP right
# so first one (0.5 0.5) is center of texture (which we will map to origin)
#
vt 0.5 0.5
#
# next 3 are for the points of the axis coords,
# the middle of the right, top, and bottom edges of the UV:
#
vt 1.0 0.5
vt 0.5 1.0
vt 0.5 0.0
#
# and these 3 should match the "help form triangles" vertices above
# (ie if you move those vertices, you should tweak these uv coords)
# imagine the Y and Z triangles folded down to lay flat with the X triangle - see diagram above
#
vt 0.5 0.80
vt 0.275 0.5
vt 0.65 0.5

#
# faces. A face is (at least) 3 points (format is v/vt/vn for each point of a face)
# The first face is the X arrow, then the Y then Z
#
f 1/2/3 4/1/3 5/5/3
f 2/3/1 4/1/1 6/6/1
f 3/4/2 4/1/2 7/7/2
